        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "[1E5•bPrP] and [1E5•2bPrP] complexes are still present, albeit in a much lower quantity. In the reference experiment (Fig. 4A), if one assumes that the peaks from the two complexes represent 100% of the intensity of the signal, the two peaks corresponding to the complexes with bPrP in the cases of peptides [140–160] and [145–165] represent only 36 and 42%, respectively, of the total intensity of all three peaks. This suggests that these peptides effectively compete with bPrP for binding with the antibody.",
          "block_bbox": [
            77,
            1186,
            591,
            1401
          ],
          "block_id": 6,
          "block_order": 1,
          "group_id": 6,
